\tag{fdip}
\title{Translation classes and continuum fields}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{The affine holonomy carries a translation class even when a
matter operator ignores every translation link. Rotations transport
that class between its appropriate quotients. This distinction also
sets the scope of comparison with continuum displacement and
rotation fields.}

